        <text class="svg-small" x="250" y="440">conflict: disjoint files, shared symbol</text>
      </svg>

      <ul class="concept-figure__fallback" aria-label="Figure summary">
        <li>The canonical graph answers which repositories and symbols depend on each other, at a named revision.</li>
        <li>The in-flight graph holds worktrees, base revisions, affected symbols, and intended publications across hosts.</li>
        <li>Joining them exposes two tasks converging on one symbol even when their file sets are disjoint.</li>
        <li>A task planned against a base revision that has since moved needs invalidating or recomputing.</li>
      </ul>

      <figcaption class="figure-caption">
        The canonical half is supported by measurement. Extending the model
